<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scanian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1675">1675</a>–<a href="/years/1679">1679</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scanian War was fought from 1675 to 1679 between Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, as part of the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a>. Denmark-Norway invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a> to recover the provinces lost in 1658 and won at sea under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niels-juel">Niels Juel</a>, but lost the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lund">Lund</a> in 1676. Under French pressure the peace treaties of 1679 restored the pre-war borders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scanian-war.jpg" alt="Scanian War" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imonoz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scanian_War_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
